---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<!-- TODO before going live (Wolfgang): check the three marked places: hosting provider, Umami location/transfer basis, retention period. -->
<Base title="Privacy" description="Privacy policy of Wolfgang Lattermann.">
  <PageHeader title="*Privacy*" />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="measure-text prose">
        <p>This page explains which data is processed when you visit this website. In short: no cookies, no forms and no ads. I use a privacy-friendly tool to see how the site is used.</p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Controller</h2>
        <p>
          Wolfgang Lattermann<br />
          Streustrasse 57<br />
          13086 Berlin<br />
          Germany<br />
          Mail <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
        </p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Hosting</h2>
        <!-- TODO: name the hosting provider and check that a data processing agreement (AVV) exists. -->
        <p>The website is run by a hosting provider in Germany, with whom a data processing agreement exists. When you open a page, the server keeps technical log data: IP address, date and time, requested file, browser and operating system. This is needed to deliver the site and keep it secure (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Log data is deleted after a short time.</p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Analytics with Umami</h2>
        <p>I use <a href="https://umami.is">Umami</a> to understand which pages are read. Umami works without cookies and without storing anything in your browser. It records: pages viewed, time on page, where the visit came from (referrer and campaign details in the address), browser, operating system, device type, screen size and approximate location (country, region). Your IP address is not stored. A visitor ID is created only from a daily changing value that cannot be reversed, and it is not used to follow you across devices.</p>
        <p>A few clicks are counted as well: the CV, email and LinkedIn links, and unlocking a protected case study (without the password you entered).</p>
        <p>The legal basis is my legitimate interest in evaluating how the site is used and how my applications perform (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). If your browser sends "Do Not Track", nothing is measured.</p>
        <!-- TODO: Umami Cloud is run by Umami Software, Inc. (USA). Check the data location and the transfer basis (standard contractual clauses / DPF) in the Umami account and name it here; or state the self-hosted server. -->
        <p>The data is processed on my behalf by Umami (Umami Software, Inc.). Data may be transferred to the USA; the basis is the EU standard contractual clauses.</p>
        <!-- TODO: set the real retention period in Umami and keep this sentence in line with it. -->
        <p>Analytics data is deleted after 12 months at the latest.</p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Personal links in applications</h2>
        <p>If you open this website through a link from one of my applications (for example <code>hallo-wl.de/companyname</code>), the link contains the name of your company. In the analytics I then see that this company visited the site, which pages were viewed and for how long. This applies to that visit only. Nothing is stored in your browser, and later visits without this link are not matched to the company. I use this to know whether an application was read (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). If you prefer not to be measured this way, open the site directly at <a href="https://hallo-wl.de">hallo-wl.de</a> or turn on "Do Not Track".</p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Protected case studies</h2>
        <p>The password for protected case studies is checked in your browser only and is not sent to a server. So that you do not have to enter it on every page, your browser remembers it until you close the tab (session storage). After that it is gone.</p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">External links</h2>
        <p>Links to LinkedIn and other sites take you away from this website. Their own privacy notices apply there.</p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Your rights</h2>
        <p>You have the right to access, correction, deletion, restriction of processing and data portability. You can object at any time to processing based on legitimate interests (Art. 21 GDPR). Write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. Because analytics data contains no names, I need details that let me find the visit, such as date and time. You can also complain to a data protection authority, for example the Berlin Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information.</p>

        <h2 class="t-heading">Changes</h2>
        <p>If the website changes, I will update this notice. Last updated: November 2026.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
